# Cut record — chain 22 (docs/deploy.md, "Cut policy"; audit v6, OPS-7). DRAFT, 2026-11-20.
#
# Drafted from deploy/cut-record.template by the cutover session (run from the build droplet). Amounts
# filled from the balances scan of 2026-11-20 (snapshot height 2 059 796).

chain-id: 22

reason: v0.8.7 runs chain 22 onward only — constraint set 11 (the cell-count gas weights with Keccak/SHA-256 lowered, Grain Poseidon2 constants made live, the per-instance quotient layout, the final EVM image with the block context, sBPF syscalls / SPL hc) changes every verifier key, every guest hc and every shielded address, so a set-11 rand-node refuses chains 14–21 at startup and no rolling update can carry it; and chain 22's genesis-gated rules need a new genesis: PST-1 (program_state.refuse_panics, monorepo#15), PERP-6 (perps.bound_payouts, monorepo#13), PERP-101 (perps.sparse_windows + max_window_heights 256, monorepo#12), multisig.max_accounts 65 536, the EVM block context (#168/#184, program_state.reference_block_window 256, Action::InvokeAt), the randomness beacon (#189: a genesis beacon section with 25 validator commitments, commit delay 256 blocks; PREVRANDAO reads it), and CON-601: validators load the pinned tier-18 state-proof key (genesis pin perps.state_proof_keys, four canonical shapes shipped beside the binary, monorepo#23), never build it — perps stays at max_tier 18 / 24 inputs (owner, 2026-11-19).

carries: the 25 validators × 1 000 RAND on chain 21's node keys (18 genesis + 7 bonded: obs1, g1–g6; same peer ids, same hosts), payouts re-derived at their set-11 addresses from each payout key; the bridge state from the chain-21 snapshot at height 2 059 796 (2026-11-20T12:36:18Z, guardians and relayer stopped 12:35:19Z): burn_sequence 17, inbound floors from the endpoints' next sequences {2: 4, 3: 5, 4: 3, 5: 7}, chain 21's emitters unchanged, bridge fees 10/10 bps to a NEW set-11 wallet bridge-fee-recipient (fingerprint YMB3-Q7C7-8CEJ-0ZSA, owner decision 2026-11-20; chain 21's 89DS-4Q4X-HXSX-MBYW is set 9); locked ETH-USDT 2.021999 / BSC-USDT 23.001999 / Tron-USDT 30 / Sol-USDT 25 = 80.023998 == custody == zUSD supply, as genesis notes per ZUSD_CARRY: owner-carry 69.024998, anish-carry 10, shielded-5 0.999 (Σ 80.023998; chain 21 launched with owner 89.002999 / anish 10 / shielded-5 0.999 — the 19.978001 zUSD redeemed on chain 21 since (operator test releases to Ethereum, 1–2 Nov) is taken from the owner's share) — the owner's and Anish's zUSD is HELD in new set-11 wallets owner-carry (CY5F-KMTK-V0S7-J0TG) and anish-carry (WC5R-B7D2-GWMC-FNSD) generated by the operator (owner decision 2026-11-20: neither key is on the operator's machine and no set-11 wallet app is released yet), forwarded to them afterwards; RAND as genesis allocs to the operator wallets the balances scan found, Σ 46 431.775078887 RAND in 10 wallets (randscan-activity-w1 40 680, demo-02 1 579.958, shielded-5 989.927, shielded-3 879.983, shielded-4 839.998, shielded-2 674.996, relayer 299.976, demo-01 232.949, shielded-1 194.992, docs-programs 58.996078887) (every note store rescanned from leaf 0 against e / obs1 on 2026-11-20 — 23 stores in parallel, then the balances step with BALANCES_RESCAN=0 resuming those stores, as at chain 21); the faucet allow-list, the same 16 recipients in chain 21's order at their set-11 addresses (anish → anish-carry); the treasury multisig, 5 of 6 with six NEW signers (treasury-signer-1..6, ~/.rand-chain22/treasury.txt), its balance 100 000 RAND carried from chain 21's multisig register (multisig_rand_held, asserted equal — not new issuance); perps carried (empty: 0 accounts, 0 collateral), its genesis root re-derived under set 11 (a45d8fdab8cf7dab972e76dd6a7a18d9e82fc8210afab672a161ee60021698b4).

drops: the dropped validator archive2 (offline since about 9 Nov on the locked stg account; its 1 000 RAND chain-21 stake and any unwithdrawn rewards are not recreated); program vaults: durian.market's chain-21 AMM pool, 200 RAND + 20 000 DUR (never swapped; RDLP supply = the launch mint, no outside users), redeployed fresh on chain 22 (PROGRAM_VAULTS_DROPPED_OK=1); validator fee rewards not withdrawn, 0.012393625 RAND (register_total − genesis_staked; chain-20/21 precedent, REWARDS_DROPPED_OK=1); the shielded pool's RAND held by wallets the operator does not hold, 6 403.099083975 RAND (pool_value 52 834.874162862 − the 46 431.775078887 carried) — faucet mints and payments to users, whose notes cannot be re-created without their addresses; the tokens other than zUSD registered on chain 21 (DUR, RDLP and the docs/program examples), not bridge-backed — durian.market re-registers what it needs.

scan-floor: 187556

clients: rand CLI v0.8.7 (tag v0.8.7 at fullnode bf5aabdf, the signed release asset, constraint set 11); bridge relayer and guardians: rolled to a BR-1005 build (bridge main) at the cut, bridge PR #15 for set 11; clients repo: main 2f80ad5e (#14, set-11 wallets) plus #16 deriveKey, released with FULLNODE_TAG v0.8.7 (PR #15) right after the cut; randscan.org PR #11 and durian.market PR #2 (engine hc 482215a8…, AMM redeploy) deploy right after the cut; randbridge.org / randprotocol.org / zusd.money / the monorepo site-sync pins move to the chain-22 genesis after the cut; accepted: wallets and sites cannot prove on chain 22 until those land (as at chain 21).

second-operator: WAIVED — as at chains 20 and 21: one operator holds every validator key and every host, so no second operator exists to rebuild the genesis; cutover-fleet-chain22.sh push runs with SECOND_REBUILD_WAIVED=1 and appends `second-rebuild-waived:` below.

second-hash:

rollback: every host keeps chain 21's data dir (-ca76c276…, data-21 on the guardian hosts) and the v0.8.6 binaries as /root/rand-node.pre-c22 and /root/rand.pre-c22 plus chain 21's msauth blob as /root/msauth-vk-production.bin.pre-c22 (68facb06…, sha-checked against v0.8.6's signed SHA256SUMS) for at least a day; chain 21's history is kept from height 187 556 on hosts e and obs1 (rand-archive-2 is abandoned); the steps: the bridge stopped first, `deploy/cutover-fleet-chain22.sh quiet <genesis>` (nothing burned or minted on chain 22, else the owner decides), `halt`, `rollback`, `start`, `wait21`, then the bridge daemons' chain-21 configs restored and started; retire-chain-dirs.sh is not run until chain 22 has run a day.
